 unfulfilled life  paths make her uniquely suited to  advanced adverse jumping every rejection  every disappointment has led you  most of the action of the film takes  place in the irs universe it's here  where the worst evelyn is told that she  must confront the world's destroying joe  butupaki alpha weymouth tells her that  her mission is to counterbalance jobu's  evil with good but his boss alpha gong  isn't as confident in her potential he  orders her to kill joy her own daughter  so that jobu will no longer be a threat  to this particular universe evelyn  refuses insisting there must be another  way to rid her daughter of jobu's  influence this leads alpha gong gong to  call for reinforcements and evelyn ends  up fighting jobu jobu's cultists and the  alpha versus resistance her only ally is  alpha weymouth who occasionally jumps  into irs raymond's body to help but is  eventually killed in his own universe by  jobu rather than hanker hopes on winning  the battle evelyn deliberately pushes  her mind beyond its shattering point  evelyn's multiversal overload marks the  end of part 1 and takes us into part two  everywhere evelyn's consciousness now  bounces between a number of universes  while it's easy to consider irs evelyn  is the only real evelyn that we're  following for the rest of the film but  that's not really the case from hero  announced there's just one evelyn  there's just one mind shared across an  increasing number of possible lives  until evelyn herself reaches omniversal  consciousness we see a fair sampling of  the universes that she's inhabiting for  ease of discussion let's label the most  important ones the spine of the story  happens in the irs universe this is  where alfa raymond recruits her into the  multiversal war the party universe is  what would have happened if alpha  weymouth had never shown up in the irs  universe in the movie star universe a  young evelyn becomes an international  movie star and martial artist and  finally the most unique the hot dog  fingers universe this is where all human  beings have big limp hot dogs for  fingers and evelyn and deirdre are a  couple  as an experiment jo butupaki has used  her power over reality to create and  quote everything bagel which turns out  to be an all-consuming black hole the  resistance of the alpha verse believes  that this is a doomsday weapon but  actually jobu is planning to use the  bagel to end her own life ultimately  jobu has been in search of someone who  can ascend to her plane of existence  understand what she's going through and  maybe talk her out of destroying herself  once evelyn becomes able to jump  effortlessly between all realities  alongside her daughter she takes to  jobu's nihilistic philosophy all too  well across the multiverse evelyn starts  acting out of cruel selfish impulse  hurting those around her because why not  if there's an infinite number of  universes in which every imaginable  outcome is happening simultaneously then  there's no meaning behind any of it  nothing matters but the bagel the circle  is a very important symbol in the movie  uh to me it's about reunification in  interviews dan quan and daniel scheinert  have equated the multiverse of their  film to the experience of modern life on  the internet people who have grown up in  the digital age have a totally different  sense of scale to their world than the  generations that came before them joy  slash jobu is a grown-up millennial  who's plugged into an overwhelming feed  of constant often contradictory  information she's measured her own value  impact and suffering against a sum total  of existence and can no longer bear it  after jobu shows evelyn the everything  bagel evelyn had a dead-eyed nihilistic  meltdown that spans multiple universes  she's seen the life she could have lived  if she'd never come to this alternate  reality so she no longer has any reason  not to act on her resentment for example  deirdre shows up to the laundromats  chinese new year party with a police  escort with the intention of  repossessing the property when evelyn  smashes the front window of the  laundromat with a baseball bat it's not  just an act of defiance against deirdre  but an expression of her loathing for  the laundromat and what it represents to  her across the multiverse evelyn stops  caring about the consequences of her  actions or their effect on others she  then shuts out all these universes to  live as a rock on an earth where life  never developed because that means she  won't have to think about any of it  throughout the entire film evelyn has  been cruel and dismissive towards  weymouth she sees raymond as naive and  weak willed while we see that evelyn  could have achieved great things without  him in her life we also see the positive  results of weymouth as well especially  when it comes to ayman's philosophy of  unconditional kindness throughout the  entire film and each time evelyn barely  notices for example when evelyn stays in  the forefront he defuses a conflict with  a dissatisfied customer at the  laundromat by dancing with him even when  he draws up divorced paperwork he does  it in the hope that they'll be able to  turn their marriage around before it's  too late it's only after evelyn has  totally given up on life that she  appreciates the power of raymond's  kindness in the irs universe he refuses  to give up on evelyn even after she  stabbed him all he wants is for everyone  to stop fighting so evelyn can help  their daughter evelyn has never reached  this level of understanding with the  women she married but now she can look  back on their life together and see the  beautiful parts of their relationship  more clearly the reveal that he's not  his squirrel yeah squirrel would just  like his like cuddly sweet innocent  version of himself  at around the same time that evelyn is  reassessing her relationship with  weymouth she's approached by deidre in  the party universe waymund assault  deidre o